  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nOutside of light rain showers this evening across locations \nsouth and east of Albany, a strong cold front to our west will \nmove through eastern New York and western New England tomorrow \nmorning. Briefly ahead of the front, a few rain showers could \ndevelop for locations north of Albany. However, chances are low \nfor these light rain showers based on current forecast trends\nwith light precipitation amounts less than 0.1 inches. Behind \nthe cold front, dry conditions return and winds increase \ntomorrow morning. Breezy conditions are in store across eastern\nNew York and western New England through the afternoon hours. \nWind gusts are supported by the latest forecast to range between\n20 and 35 mph. The stronger wind gusts are still on track, from\nthis morning's forecast, to be from the Mohawk Valley to the \nCapital Region and the Berkshires. Make sure to secure any \noutdoor loose objects as they could be blown around due to the \nbreezy conditions tomorrow. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nWhile Monday night into Tuesday morning is going to be chilly \nwith lows in the upper 20s for high terrain locations and upper \n30s to low 40s for valley locations, light winds will be \npreventing any frost development in valley locations. Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday morning is still supported by the latest \nforecast to bring calm winds and clear skies for patchy frost to\ndevelop in the upper Hudson Valley region. At this forecast \ntime, confidence is low on how widespread and impactful frost \nwill be in valley locations as the center of the high pressure \nsystem is trending further south from eastern New York. Low \ntemperatures range in the low to upper 30s. For reference, the \nnormal low temperature for the beginning of October in Albany is\nbetween 44 and 46 degrees. Low temperatures could range between\n5 to 10 degrees below normal for this time of year across \neastern New York and western New England. At least through \nWednesday morning as we return to near normal low temperatures \nfor Wednesday night into Thursday morning that continues through\nthe end of the work week.",
